    "name": "Netherlands",
    "instrument": "RDW — Exchanging a foreign driving licence (countries outside EU/EFTA with agreement)",
    "source_url": "https://www.rdw.nl/en/driving-licence/foreign-driving-licence/exchanging-a-foreign-driving-licence",
    "source_urls": [
      "https://www.rdw.nl/en/driving-licence/foreign-driving-licence/exchanging-a-foreign-driving-licence"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "EU/EFTA licences exchange under separate mutual rules (not listed as third-country agreement rows).",
      "For non-EU/EFTA licences, RDW requires the holder lived in the issuing country for 185 days in the year the licence was obtained.",
      "Exchange requires registration in the Dutch BRP (Personal Records Database) and other RDW conditions.",
      "30% ruling expats may exchange a licence from any country under a separate scheme — not modelled as a general annex row."
    ]
  },
